      {
        "review_id": 675812990,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r675812990-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Hated it",
        "text": "I didn't like this temple because I felt like the people in the temple, the alleged \"holy men\" included, are using the temple to make a quick buck out of tourists. This ruined the experience for me, even though the temple and the rituals being performed were interesting. \n\nAfter I bought a ticket, a guide followed me in. I assumed it was because some parts of the temple were off limits to tourists so he needed to flag that out. He ended up giving us a tour of the temple, which was helpful. However at the end of the tour, he was very pushy about the \"tip\". He asked for USD20 per person! We gave him USD 3 each because it was a short tour (about 1 HR), and also because we didn't have much money on us. In the end I had to show him my wallet to let him know that I had no money at all on me and I was giving him everything I had.\n\nAs for the \"holy men\", I was told they gave up family and material possessions to live as monks in the temple. However after we took photos with them, they asked for money. Bearing in mind I had only USD 4 in my wallet, I gave him USD 1 and he was unhappy, asking for \"more money\". At that point, I walked away but I no longer felt safe in the temple. \n\n",
