        "title": "Interesting observance of Hindu rituals",
        "text": "Being of Irish lineage, funerals were one of the few times my family got together and it was generally a memorable and fun experience.  When I share these experiences with others outside my family, they always look at me funny and its obvious they do something different.  As a result, I've always had a curiosity about how other cultures deal with a loved one's passing.\nWell, a Hindu cremation is much more ritualistic, serene and reverent.  It was worthwhile to have a guide explain the process both before, during and after the event.  I found it moving.  There were several pyres at various stages and you could walk along the river and observe.  \nThere were monkeys around trying to get food where they could find it.  There were several priests offering their services for a fee.  \nI would recommend going if you have an interest and be respectful.",
