      {
        "review_id": 673144369,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r673144369-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "an outworldy experience (for a westerner) inthe nepali varanasi.",
        "text": "we are so jaded today that even the sight of human bodies consumed on pyres is for most tourists no more than a good photo op but this is one of nepal's unmissable points.\ncome early morning- but anytime is good- and with plenty of time to walk the maze of shivalingas, temples and burning sites beside the polluted bagmati river as you are surrounded by leaping monkeys, posing sadhus, hindu priests and worshippers.\nthe main temple is out of bounds for non hindus but its a small fraction of the area.\nkeep your shoes on! its allowed and you dont want an infection in such a place.\nyou can stand right beside the grieving families and watch the bodies but be respectful about taking photos.\ndespite the millions pouring into the place, toilets are very scarce. use the one near the shoe deposit area.\nentrance is 1000 npr. guides are waiting there too.",
