        "title": "Pashupatinath Temple",
        "text": "No visitor to Kanthmandu would like to miss the opportunity to visit the Pashupatinath site, which is so richly endowed with places to see and stuff to buy. There are temples and idols so esoteric and monumental for the lenses of their cameras.\nThe temple is about 5km from the city. To get there, one can hire a taxi or ride on a minibus or tempo. The Pashupatinath temple symbolizes Nepal's national glory. It is the centre of faith and relgious piety for the Hindus and Buddhists of the world, as well as a unique treasure that forms part of the world heritage.",
