        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r671533246-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Not really a place for foreigners",
        "text": "We visited here in April 2019. In our opinion, it was not worth it. Being foreigners and non-Hindu, we were very limited to where we could go. I understand the religious significance of the site and appreciate it.  Just didn’t feel welcomed there. It’s a lot of money to watch a cremation, which we personally felt was an intrusion on a private moment, so we didn’t. Left with a feeling of our money was wanted, but not us.  Holy men are located throughout the areas where foreigners are allowed and for a price will bestow a blessing. The monkeys were very aggressive.  The  Buddhist stupas were by far better places to visit.  ",
        "review_tip": null,
